speak with you today,

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:23.160
specifically about TPUs
and TensorFlow on Kaggle.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.620
But first, what's Kaggle?

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.510
Historically, Kaggle's
become synonymous

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:29.550
with machine learning
competitions,

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.720
but it's really much,
much more than that.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.080
Kaggle is a data
science platform.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.210
Over five million
data scientists

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.203
from all over the world
come to Kaggle not only

00:00:39.203 --> 00:00:41.370
to participate in the machine
learning competitions,

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.880
but to learn data science,
build their skills,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.810
polished their portfolios,
and share data sets and code.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:52.402
It's truly an incredibly
exciting community.

00:00:52.402 --> 00:00:56.100
Now my job at Kaggle is to run
machine learning competitions,

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.140
and they run the gamut.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.750
Right now we have 17
competitions running,

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.320
ranging from understanding
bird sounds, [INAUDIBLE] lung

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:07.420
